WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.421
Week 3: Objects, Gender, and the Classroom. identify people and objects ask what something is follow basic instructions

2
00:00:08.421 --> 00:00:15.817
Cultural lens. Academic schedules, grading language, and forms of address across Spanish-speaking schools.

3
00:00:15.817 --> 00:00:28.251
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:28.251 --> 00:00:40.259
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:40.259 --> 00:00:49.471
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:49.471 --> 00:01:12.359
Model language. Hay un libro sobre la mesa. — There is a book on the table. ¿Qué es esto? — What is this? Es una pregunta importante. — It is an important question. Abran los cuadernos, por favor. — Open your notebooks, please. Las respuestas están en la página diez. — The answers are on page ten.

7
00:01:12.359 --> 00:01:22.513
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
